  "title": "why starting the viewer is ambiguous, and what it costs to make it not be",
  "source": "code-read",
  "source_detail": "viewer/server.js's start path, viewer/test/helpers/server.js:88 and :97, viewer/test/server.test.js:1094, protocol/graphs.md's start recipe, IDEA.md:100; Q1 of this plan, raised by review round 1",
  "explanation": "One command has two behaviours and nothing says which you got, which is the only reason the recipe has to background it and poll a log. What changed since this was last drawn is the box about what assumes the launched process is the server: it is five places, not one, and two of them inject code into that process to freeze the lockfile race, which no pid lookup can repair. Weigh [the three ways out](#the-two-ways) against that. Leaves out --show and --stop, which none of them touch.",
